
📘 SQL Learning Repository
🐬 Project Overview

The SQL Learning Repository is a complete collection of SQL practice files, datasets, and notes created while learning MySQL and PL/SQL.
It includes hands-on exercises involving table creation, constraints, joins, functions, indexing, subqueries, and PL/SQL programming.

This repository is useful for:

Students learning SQL

Data analysts practicing MySQL

Interview preparation

Beginners to advance who want step-by-step SQL scripts

🎯 Objective

This project was created to:

Practice SQL fundamentals and advanced concepts through structured .sql files

Understand database operations such as joins, constraints, and indexing

Learn PL/SQL logic including loops, conditions, and procedures

Use real datasets (company.xlsx, BigData.xlsx, joins.xlsx) for practical query building

Maintain all SQL learning resources in a single organized repository

📂 Project Structure
SQL-Learning/
├── 1_MySQL_CreateTable_BasicQueries.sql
├── 2_SQL_Constraints_AlterTable.sql
├── 3_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part1.sql
├── 4_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part2.sql
├── 5_Index_View_Subquery_Joins.sql
├── 6_SQL_Functions_Numerical_String_Date_Coalesce_Case.sql
├── 7_PLSQL_Variables_Loops_Procedures_Functions.sql
│
├── BigData.xlsx
├── company.xlsx
├── joins.xlsx
│
└── MYSQL WORKBENCH INSTALLATION.doc

🛠️ Approach
1. SQL Basics

Creating databases & tables

Inserting, updating, deleting data

Basic SELECT queries

2. Constraints & Alter Table

Primary key, Foreign key

Unique, Not Null, Default

Modifying columns using ALTER TABLE

3. Joins & Auto-Increment

AUTO_INCREMENT usage

INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL joins

Join-based real dataset queries (joins.xlsx)

4. Advanced SQL Features

Creating views

Indexing for performance

Subqueries (single-row & multi-row)

Nested queries

5. SQL Functions

Numerical functions

String functions

Date & time functions

COALESCE

CASE expressions

6. PL/SQL Concepts

Variables and constants

IF/ELSE blocks

Loops (FOR, WHILE)

Arrays & collections

Procedures and functions

🧪 Datasets Included

Three Excel datasets are included for practicing queries:

📊 1. BigData.xlsx

Used for large table operations, filtering, grouping, and analytics.

🧑‍💼 2. company.xlsx

Employee- or department-based data for joins, conditions, and functions.

🔗 3. joins.xlsx

A lightweight dataset specifically for practicing various join operations.

🧰 MySQL Workbench Installation

A complete installation guide is provided:

📄 MYSQL WORKBENCH INSTALLATION.doc
This includes step-by-step instructions with screenshots to set up MySQL Server + Workbench.

🚀 Getting Started
1. Install MySQL Server + Workbench

Open the Word file:

MYSQL WORKBENCH INSTALLATION.doc


Follow the complete setup instructions.

2. Run SQL Files

Execute the .sql scripts one by one in MySQL Workbench:

Basics

Constraints

Joins

Indexing

Functions

PL/SQL scripts

3. Use Excel Data for Practice

Import the .xlsx files into MySQL using:

Table import wizard

OR manual LOAD DATA steps

🧩 Sample Query Topics Covered

Creating tables & inserting rows

Selecting specific & filtered data

Joining multiple tables

Aggregation functions

Subqueries

Creating consistent Data Models

PL/SQL loops & conditions

🧠 Troubleshooting
❗ Query Error

Check whether tables exist and names match.

❗ Foreign Key Issues

Ensure referenced tables are created before applying constraints.

❗ Import Issues with Excel

Convert .xlsx → .csv if MySQL version does not support direct Excel import.

❗ Low Understanding of Joins

Refer to 3_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part1.sql and 3_AutoIncrement_Joins_Part2.sql.

📈 Learning Outcomes

By practicing this repository, you will learn:

How SQL databases work

How to write clean, optimized queries

How to perform analysis on real datasets

Fundamentals of relational database design

Basics of PL/SQL programming

